    },
    {
      "start_time": 330,
      "end_time": 362,
      "annotation": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "After kicking the dirt into Jude's face and fruit, Nicasia implies that she is from dirt, and to dirt she will return. This is further setting up Jude's place in society. She is considered dirt to the Faeries, who are immortal, and she will eventually die, and be buried in dirt. The Fae have little regard for mortals. "
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
